# Where the built frontend looks for the verifier.
#
# Read only by `vite build` (mode=production). `vite dev` never loads this
# file, so local work keeps using the `/api` default and the dev-server proxy
# in vite.config.js — the two setups do not interfere.
#
# This is checked in on purpose. It is a public address, not a credential, and
# holding it here rather than in a hosting dashboard means the repository
# builds into a working demo for anyone who clones it. A value that lives only
# in a control panel is a value nobody can review.
#
# Why a separate host rather than the frontend's own /api:
#
# The claim flow is five requests — capture, open gate, verify, enrol, settle —
# that must all agree about one gate and one roster. Serverless gives each
# invocation its own filesystem, so those five can land on five instances with
# five databases. Measured on the previous all-in-one deployment: four
# enrolments reported a roster of two, and the console contradicted itself in
# the same view, offering "2 enrolled" beside "compared against 1 of 1".
#
# store.py guards writes with a threading.RLock. That is real mutual exclusion
# inside one process and nothing at all between them, and its own docstring
# notes that interleaved appends fork the hash chain — so verify_chain would
# report tampering that never happened. One process, one file is the condition
# the store was written for, so the backend runs as one process.
VITE_XANO_API_BASE=https://stratum-verifier.onrender.com
